Gap: `str::starts_with("cnt")` in `Table::count_columns` - Aeneas stops in `core::str::pattern` (`[Error] Unimplemented`), and the extraction fails
The column's name is matched as bytes: `as_bytes().starts_with(b"cnt")`. A `str` starts with an
ASCII prefix exactly when its UTF-8 bytes start with the prefix's bytes. On top of patch 01,
which made `count_columns` a loop.
Tests: no test calls `count_columns` directly. layout::tests::stack_offsets_fit_at_size_limits
builds the layout through it; `-p stable_lean_vm_core --test verifiers`.
mutation: the prefix `b"cnx"`, so that no column counts -> both fail.

diff --git a/crates/verifier/src/layout.rs b/crates/verifier/src/layout.rs
index 1037c18ef..3784f2555 100644
--- a/crates/verifier/src/layout.rs
+++ b/crates/verifier/src/layout.rs
@@ -217,7 +217,7 @@ impl Table {
     fn count_columns(&self) -> Vec<usize> {
         let mut columns = Vec::new();
         for i in 0..self.width() {
-            if self.columns[i].starts_with("cnt") {
+            if self.columns[i].as_bytes().starts_with(b"cnt") {
                 columns.push(i);
             }
         }
